<title>INDIA: No brake on bank loans to finance firms, says RBI.</title>
<headline>No brake on bank loans to finance firms, says RBI.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Reserve Bank of India (RBI) on Tuesday said it had not issued any directive to banks to curtail bank loans to non-bank finance companies (NBFCs).</p>
<p>&quot;A section of the press had ...reported that the RBI had issued a directive to banks to put a brake on credit enhancement to all non-bank financial companies (NBFCs),&quot; RBI said.</p>
<p>The RBI said there was no quantitative ceiling on bank finance to equipment leasing and hire purchase companies that had complied with RBI requirements on registration, credit rating and prudential norms and have been so certified.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
